Running tests with a ros2 serial node:

Build the test node
1. cd rover_workspace/src/arm_controls/serial_communication_library/testing/ros2_serial_test
2. colcon build --packages-select serial_ros2_testing
3. . install/setup.bash

Launch armjoy
4. make sure the joystick is connected to the vm
5. open another terminal
6. cd rover_workspace/src/robotic_arm_controls/launch
7. ros2 launch arm_joy.launch.xml

Upload test sketch to the arduino
8. open the arduino ide
9. open test.ino found in rover_workspace/src/arm_controls/serial_communication_library/testing/arduino_sketch/test
10. verify and upload

Finally start the test node
11. ros2 run serial_ros2_testing listener

This node subscribes to the /arm_joy topic. It publishs the axes of the joystick to the arduino to which the arduino should simply 
write them back.

C++ Joy message: https://docs.ros.org/en/melodic/api/sensor_msgs/html/msg/Joy.html

--------------------------------------------------------

Running basic unit tests to check serial read and write:

1. cd rover_workspace/src/arm_controls/serial_communication_library/build
2. make
3. ./serial_comms_tests
